      "id": "945fdd28-160f-4d9b-80e7-e3d96acf858d",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 4,
      "data": {
        "title": "Secrets: onde eles morram"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "76d4b3db-9a3c-43f4-9a23-51f806021468",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "language": "bash",
            "code": "# Pre-commit hook: trufflehog ou gitleaks bloqueia secret antes do commit\n# .pre-commit-config.yaml\n- repo: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks\n  rev: v8.18.0\n  hooks:\n    - id: gitleaks\n\n# CI\n- name: Scan for secrets\n  uses: gitleaks/gitleaks-action@v2\n  env:\n    GITHUB_TOKEN: ${'$'}{{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}\n\n# Em runtime (Node + AWS)\nimport { SecretsManagerClient, GetSecretValueCommand } from '@aws-sdk/client-secrets-manager';\nconst client = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: 'us-east-1' });\nconst secret = await client.send(new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId: 'prod/db/password' }));\n// nunca console.log(secret), nunca persiste em disco"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "e5c65cad-8879-4525-ada0-2c168244f522",
          "type": "callout",
          "position": 1,
          "data": {
            "variant": "danger",
            "title": "",
            "content": "Red flags. (1) no repo. (2) em dev deixado em prod. (3) Secret como variável de build que fica no histórico do Docker ( com senha → use ). (4) Token de service account com TTL infinito."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "90dfda20-59eb-4a37-ad6f-b32faf368940",
      "type": "section",
      "position": 5,
      "data": {
        "title": "Supply Chain: SBOM, SLSA, Sigstore"
      },
      "children": [
        {
          "id": "aea46a89-4e40-4f08-9d41-a69703fe75f1",
          "type": "code_block",
          "position": 0,
          "data": {
            "language": "bash",
            "code": "# Gerar SBOM\nsyft packages dir:. -o cyclonedx-json > sbom.json\n\n# Scan de vuln contra SBOM\ngrype sbom:./sbom.json --fail-on high\n\n# Assinar imagem Docker\ncosign sign --key cosign.key ghcr.io/empresa/app:${SHA}\n\n# Verificar na hora do deploy (policy de admission)\ncosign verify --key cosign.pub ghcr.io/empresa/app:${SHA}"
          }
        }
      ]
